#          <li><b>On staging</b> <span>v2.63.7, replacing v2.63: everything v2.63 carried (the wire fix, a mask's own colour mixer, the first stage of the mask work, the LUT grid and None for looks), plus a picked mask's own grade and Sky band, a line under "Editing" saying dimmed controls stay with the whole photo, new masks that change nothing until a control is moved, and double-tap that puts a mask's slider back to no change and is no longer lost while the photo redraws. It waits on your device pass; the steps are in NOTES.</span></li>
# -        <li><b>Built and held</b> <span>Nothing. The mask work's stage 2b goes on after the device pass and your Aerochrome answer.</span></li>
# -        <li><b>Last verified green</b> <span><code>ec29ded</code>: the Gates run and the deploy for that exact commit both passed. A page cannot carry the identifier of the commit that writes it, so this always names the one before.</span></li>
# +        <li><b>Built and held</b> <span>Nothing. The Aerochrome work now leads the queue, ahead of the rest of the mask work: the sky selection behind the halo (052), the round spots (013), the fill for sky inside a lattice (065), Aerochrome rendered from a model of the film (066), red and blue lining up at thin edges (061), and the two-photo route (067). The mask work's stage 2b follows.</span></li>
# +        <li><b>Last verified green</b> <span><code>b7ce1ee</code>: the Gates run and the deploy for that exact commit both passed. A page cannot carry the identifier of the commit that writes it, so this always names the one before.</span></li>
#          <li><b>Next version</b> <span>2.63 is the staged build's number, because masks gain their own amounts in it. The next release that adds something takes 2.64.</span></li>
#        </ul>
#  
# @@ -102,25 +102,32 @@
#              colour mixer, the LUT grid, None, "Add to it", and the test page's
#              timing with eight masks).
#            </li>
# -          <li>
# -            <strong>Which the Aerochrome button should be</strong>: as shipped, or
# -            Pink IR with your Sky and Foliage band values plus Aerochrome's own
# -            denoise. The pictures went with the question: the second has no round
# -            spots, a deeper sky and crimson grass, and a slightly more textured sky
# -            at full size.
# -          </li>
# -          <li>
# -            <strong>Whether the look's sky should read your Sky mask next</strong>
